## Regularization Methods

### L1 and L2 Regularization

#### L2 Regularization (Weight Decay)

**Effect**: Penalizes large weights, encourages simplicity.

$$L_{regularized} = L + \lambda \sum_i w_i^2$$

**Gradient with L2**:
$$\frac{\partial L_{reg}}{\partial w} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial w} + 2\lambda w$$

```python
# L2 regularization in model
model = tf.keras.Sequential([
    tf.keras.layers.Dense(
        128,
        activation='relu',
        kernel_regularizer=tf.keras.regularizers.L2(l2=0.001),
        input_shape=(784,)
    ),
    tf.keras.layers.Dense(
        10,
        activation='softmax',
        kernel_regularizer=tf.keras.regularizers.L2(l2=0.001)
    )
])

# Or via optimizer (weight_decay in AdamW)
optimizer = optimizers.AdamW(learning_rate=0.001, weight_decay=0.01)
```

#### L1 Regularization (Sparse Weights)

**Effect**: Encourages sparse weights (feature selection).

$$L_{regularized} = L + \lambda \sum_i |w_i|$$

```python
model = tf.keras.Sequential([
    tf.keras.layers.Dense(
        128,
        activation='relu',
        kernel_regularizer=tf.keras.regularizers.L1(l1=0.001),
